# Copy this file to .env and fill in your values.
# Never commit your actual .env file — it is gitignored.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTHING HERE IS REQUIRED TO RUN THE DASHBOARD.
# The four setup commands in README.md work on a fresh clone with no .env file
# at all. You only need a key to talk to the AI agent.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LLM API key — read by the agent in lib/agent/
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Set the one matching the provider configured in lib/agent/. Without it the
# dashboard and the whole REST API still work; only /chat is unavailable.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_key_here

# Alternatives, if the agent is pointed at a different provider:
# OPENAI_API_KEY=your_key_here
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=your_key_here
# GROQ_API_KEY=your_key_here


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database — no variable needed
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# There is deliberately no DATABASE_URL here. prisma/schema.prisma hardcodes
# the SQLite path ("file:./dev.db") so that a fresh clone runs with zero env
# setup and the judges' commands cannot fail on a missing .env.
#
# The database file lives at prisma/dev.db and is gitignored. To reset it to
# the shipped seed data at any time, run `npm run seed`.
#
# If we ever move off SQLite, switch the datasource in prisma/schema.prisma
# back to env("DATABASE_URL") and add that variable here.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NODE_ENV — set automatically
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# lib/db.ts reads NODE_ENV to decide how loudly Prisma logs and whether to
# reuse the client across hot reloads. Next.js sets it for you
# ("development" for `npm run dev`, "production" for `npm run build`), so do
# not set it here.
